why Every Alliance quest of Uldaman in one run, lead-ins included.

# Uldaman's Alliance quests in one guide: the pick-ups and lead-ins between
# Ironforge, Loch Modan and the Badlands (for Mages their Power in Uldaman
# chain too), the work in the Badlands and the caves before the door, one run,
# then the hand-ins. Steps already done are passed over, so the guide picks up
# wherever the chain stands.
#
# The chains:
# - The Crumpled Map's 720 A Sign of Hope -> Prospector Ryedol's 721 (to
#   Hammertoe Grez) -> 722 Amulet of Secrets -> 723 Prospect of Faith -> 724 (to
#   Historian Karnik) -> 725 -> 726 -> 762 An Ambassador of Evil -> Advisor
#   Belgrum's 1139 The Lost Tablets of Will (inside).
# - Prospector Stormpike's 707 Ironband Wants You! -> Prospector Ironband's
#   738 Find Agmond -> 739 Murdaloc -> 704 Agmond's Fate (Carved Stone Urns).
# - Ghak Healtouch's 2500 Badlands Reagent Run -> 17 Uldaman Reagent Run.
# - Prospector Stormpike's 2398 The Lost Dwarves -> Baelog's 2240 The Hidden
#   Chamber (inside).
# - The Shattered Necklace (item 7666) starts 2198 -> Talvash del Kissel's
#   2199 Lore for a Price -> 2200 Back to Uldaman -> the Remains of a Paladin's
#   2201 Find the Gems -> 2204 Restoring the Necklace (both at Talvash's
#   Scrying Bowl, which his Phial of Scrying calls up inside) -> 2361.
# - Krom Stoutarm's 1360 Reclaimed Treasures; Rigglefuzz's 2418 Power Stones;
#   Theldurin the Lost's 709 Solution to Doom; the Discs of Norgannon's 2278 ->
#   2279 The Platinum Discs (to High Explorer Magellas) -> 2439 (to Dinita
#   Stonemantle).
# - Mages: 1953 Return to the Marsh -> Tabetha's 1954 The Infernal Orb ->
#   1955 The Exorcism -> 1956 Power in Uldaman (the Obsidian Sentinel's power
#   source).
#
# Left out: 1192 Indurium Ore and 3375 Replacement Phial (repeatable), with
# Indurium Ore's racing-camp chain (1104 to 1194); the Mages' 1957 Mana
# Surges and the Platinum Discs' 2963, the next steps beyond.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses, Baelog, the Remains or the
# objects inside, so their goals stand at the door (@44.6,12.1, Badlands)
# with `group 5`. The bosses come in the order of the client's dungeon
# journal (Revelosh, the Lost Dwarves, Ironaya, the Obsidian Sentinel, the
# Ancient Stone Keeper, Galgann Firehammer, Grimlok, Archaedas), not of a
# recorded run. Every quest goal is counted by the quest log, so a group that
# takes them in another order still gets each step ticked. Hammertoe Grez,
# the chests and the urns stand in the caves on the Badlands map, before the
# door.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. Talvash's Scrying Bowl is an object inside
#   Uldaman there; Find the Gems' text says the Phial of Scrying calls him.
# - The door: players' recordings, as Polestar's Codex holds them
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   41 to 51).
# - Mob levels from data/forever set the waits: Murdaloc 42, the Stonevault
#   Bonesnappers 39 to 40; Magregan Deepshadow and Ambassador Infernus are
#   elites.
# - Lint warns that the door is more than 50 yards from the Magenta Cap
#   Clusters outside; the goal stays at the door for the ones inside.
# INGAME: where inside do Baelog, the Remains of a Paladin, the Discs of
#   Norgannon and the Tablet of Will stand?

